  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-17T23:40:21.428Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So this is two things really and both relate to using the Chat Box with OSC. \ni know of a STT program that works with the new Chat Box and i have also just made my own using assembly ai, and while it works pretty well i actually have no idea what STT is putting in my own chat box. There needs to be a option to view what's currently in your own text box without having to look straight up every 5 seconds, its hurting my neck and it breaks the flow when talking to people. im thinking a window attached to the hand or something on hud.\n\nThe other thing is it would be great if when other people put something in their textbox you could read it with OSC. I'm thinking alone the lines of /chatbox/output s1 s2 where s1 is the player name and s2 is the message. This would allow creation of a TTS program to read out other users chatboxes, something that I personally want to make.\nI know you guys plan on adding you own STT and TTS systems but in the mean time this would be a massive help.",
